>
>   1)  Anything important about the statues or fountains?  I have found
>   out that there are nasties in  some but any incentive to drink at
>   every one?  What do you do with the statues of the different
>   monsters?

	Statues will turn into that type of monster sometimes, when
walked on, or when other things are done to them.  Better yet, when
broken up with a pickaxe, there is a fairly good chance that you find
a spellbook inside.  Fountains are best for a) uncursing cursed stuff
("The water glows for a moment"), b) getting Excalibur (You have to be
above level 5, but #dip the sword, and watch as the murky hand makes
it for you), c) slim chance of getting a wish (quaff).

>   2)  How do you steal from shop keepers in this version.  Telporting
>   or digging doesn't seem to work as well as it used to?

	The best way is to dig a diagonal hole thru the wall and kick
stuff through.  No biggie.  Otherwise, let your pet pick it up, and
when he/she drops it in front of you, feed him/her.

>   3)  What is the word to engrave to keep the monsters away?

	Elbereth.

